+## Offline Replay and Reproducible Runs
+
+The evaluator can replay a request-ID-keyed LLM response cassette without an API key. Replay mode fails closed on any request ID that is absent from the cassette and disables the guest NIC by default.
+
+Run the checked-in end-to-end smoke fixture (QEMU + VTRM + World Effect Judge, no model API calls):
+
+```bash
+bash scripts/test/run_offline_smoke.sh
+```
+
+To record a live run for future replay, configure the normal model credentials and pass `--record-file`:
+
+```bash
+python3 judge/run_vtrm_eval.py \
+  --tasks-dir judge/tasks_should_pass \
+  --task-id 301-workspace-hello \
+  --record-file runtime/replays/301-workspace-hello.json
+```
+
+Then replay it offline:
+
+```bash
+python3 judge/run_vtrm_eval.py \
+  --tasks-dir judge/tasks_should_pass \
+  --task-id 301-workspace-hello \
+  --replay-file runtime/replays/301-workspace-hello.json \
+  --no-guest-network
+```
+
+See [`judge/replays/README.md`](judge/replays/README.md) for cassette format, audit logs, and networking caveats. Replay runs write `replay_ok` into `summary.json` and record the cassette SHA-256 in `run_manifest.json`.
+
+### Representative offline benchmark
+
+Run a six-task deterministic suite covering three benign workspace operations and three security-denial cases (read-only database update, audit-log insert, and read-only database delete):
+
+```bash
+PYTHON=/path/to/python bash scripts/test/run_offline_representative_suite.sh
+```
+
+The script runs the benign and denial groups separately so the evaluator preserves its existing `tasks_should_fail` classification, disables guest networking, verifies VTRM denial audit records, and writes `runtime/offline-representative/offline_benchmark.json` plus a Markdown summary. Timing statistics are derived from terminal VTRM audit events and exclude model inference latency; they are not full end-to-end task latency. See `judge/replays/README.md` for cassette and report details.
+
+For a repeated performance study (three repetitions by default), use:
+
+```bash
+PYTHON=/path/to/python bash scripts/test/run_offline_repeated_benchmark.sh
+```
+
+This records separate QEMU launch/readiness, guest-agent bootstrap, initial image copy, per-case image reset, task-wait, and terminal VTRM audit timings. It writes a host/environment manifest and aggregates mean, median, p95, minimum, and maximum to `runtime/offline-repeated/<study-id>/repeated_benchmark.md` and `.json`. Override `REPETITIONS=5` for a larger sample. Boot readiness uses one-second log polling; VTRM timings exclude model inference and full end-to-end task latency.
+
