+# AgentOS artifact and reproduction guide
+
+## Artifact identity
+
+This experimental software overlay is reconstructed from the public AgentOS baseline and a reviewable patch:
+
+- Upstream repository: https://github.com/zhoujune/AgentOS
+- Upstream commit: 4147c7f780ccb59b83f3dba8da5f19e73a1d1a8c
+- Upstream tree: a19299570fa796795c8e0cf787f29c41718ae960
+- Companion overlay patch: patches/0001-agentos-offline-replay-overlay.patch in the AgentOS Software Impacts companion repository.
+- Patch checksum: recorded in the companion repository provenance manifest.
+
+This is a pinned reconstruction candidate, **not yet a tagged release**. The overlay adds deterministic offline replay, validation, and repeated-benchmark scripts. It does not include local-model weights or the separate PPU local-inference experiment.
+
+## Host requirements
+
+The tested host environment was Ubuntu 24.04.2 LTS, Python 3.12.3, QEMU 8.2.2, e2fsprogs 1.47.0 (debugfs and e2fsck), and OpenJDK 21.0.12.1 for TLC. The host kernel reported by the server was 5.10.134-17.2.al8.x86_64. The packaged guest kernel is Linux 6.12.47.
+
+The offline evaluator, LLM proxy, validator, aggregator, and their tests use the Python standard library. The optional Streamlit UI declares streamlit>=1.44,<2 in packages/requirements-streamlit-ui.txt; Streamlit was not installed on the host used for the offline validation, so the UI was not part of that test.
+
+For the formal model, Java and the included packages/tla2tools.jar are required. The bundled TLC version is 2.19 (8 August 2024).
+
+To rebuild guest images, the README requires a separate compatible buildroot-2026.02 checkout next to this repository. The full Buildroot source is **not vendored**, and its exact Git commit and package revisions are not recorded in the current artifact. The supplied images can be used without rebuilding.
+
+## Supplied images
+
+| Image | SHA-256 |
+| --- | --- |
+| artifacts/images/bzImage | 2e7101b6ce88b5b7c27b8bc3ecee0d48c2db97992900539d75784397ca11436d |
+| artifacts/images/rootfs.eval.clean.ext2 | d61a40dc7f2090b19505886020593674cdf2b5dd2f85fbcb9c02c523745a5f61 |
+
+The clean evaluation rootfs passed read-only e2fsck -fn validation. The production rootfs was not used in this smoke workflow.
+
+## Reproduction commands
+
+Run from the repository root after applying the companion overlay patch.
+
+### 1. Unit tests
+
+~~~bash
+python3 -m unittest discover -s judge -p 'test_*.py' -v
+~~~
+
+### 2. One-task offline QEMU smoke
+
+~~~bash
+bash scripts/test/run_offline_smoke.sh
+~~~
+
+This uses a hand-authored request-ID-keyed cassette, does not require a model API key, disables the guest NIC, and checks task completion, safety, and exact replay matching. Set OUTPUT_ROOT=/path/to/output to change the output directory.
+
+### 3. Six-task deterministic representative suite
+
+~~~bash
+bash scripts/test/run_offline_representative_suite.sh
+~~~
+
+The cassette covers three benign workspace tasks and three direct database-denial tasks. It is a small software regression fixture, not the full 24-benign/48-adversarial ASE evaluation.
+
+### 4. Repeated offline benchmark
+
+~~~bash
+REPETITIONS=3 bash scripts/test/run_offline_repeated_benchmark.sh
+~~~
+
+The runner executes complete six-task rounds and aggregates stage timings. For the controlled A/B comparison and its limits, see the companion repository's docs/CONTROLLED_BENCHMARK_20261031.md.
+
+### 5. Abstract TLA+ model check
+
+~~~bash
+java -cp packages/tla2tools.jar tlc2.TLC \
+  -config formal/vtrm_core.cfg formal/vtrm_core.tla
+~~~
+
+The check completed with 5,563 states generated, 103 distinct states, and no model-checking error. This result applies only to the finite abstract model described in formal/README.md; it does not prove the Python implementation or end-to-end VM execution correct.
+
+## Validation observed on 2026-11-01
+
+- Unit discovery: 11 tests passed.
+- Canonical offline QEMU smoke: one case passed; task_completion_ok, safety_ok, replay_ok, and all_ok were all true.
+- Clean evaluation rootfs: e2fsck -fn passed.
+- TLC 2.19: 5,563 states generated, 103 distinct, no error.
+- The separate six-task A/B experiment completed three repetitions per profile (36/36 task executions passed); its comparison is descriptive and sequential, not randomized.
+- A separate two-task local PPU live-model smoke is documented in the companion repository and is not part of this default reproduction path.
+
+## Known reproducibility gaps
+
+1. Buildroot 2026.02 is external; its exact source commit and package configuration lock are missing.
+2. The optional Streamlit dependency is a version range, not a full transitive lock.
+3. No permanent archive/capsule identifier or tagged software release exists yet.
+4. The upstream repository has no root LICENSE file. The ASE conference artifact page states MIT licensing; add the complete license text with a verified copyright notice before release.
+5. The six-task cassette is not the original 72-task live-model evaluation.
+
+Do not describe this artifact as fully reproducible until the remaining source, license, dependency, and archival items are closed.
